# Citation metadata for the local research artifact.
# No public repository URL, personal author identity, DOI, release date, or
# software version was supplied. These fields are deliberately omitted.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use cagra-chunksplice, its experimental design, diagram, or recorded
  results in scholarly work, please cite this software and the relevant upstream
  works in references. Identify the exact source digest or archived revision.
  Publication citation is a scholarly expectation, not an additional MIT
  license condition.
type: software
title: "cagra-chunksplice: Controlled Experiments on Intra-Chunk Connectivity in Incremental Proximity Graphs"
authors:
  - family-names: "Çalışır"
    given-names: "Cihan"
    email: "calisircihan21@gmail.com"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A modular PyTorch mechanism experiment comparing exact graph rebuilding,
  snapshot insertion with degree-capped reverse edges, intra-chunk nearest-neighbor
  splicing, and optional bounded local relative-neighborhood refinement.
  Recorded artifacts comprise a controlled insertion-partition sweep and a
  four-update stream using synthetic drift microclusters on an NVIDIA GeForce
  RTX 4070 SUPER. This is not an implementation or benchmark of NVIDIA
  cuVS/CAGRA, the complete MIRAGE-ANNS index, or HNSW.
keywords:
  - approximate nearest neighbor search
  - proximity graphs
  - incremental indexing
  - GPU
  - PyTorch
  - chunk splicing
  - reproducibility
